-- ccc2-drilling-entry.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), PART II, ss 70 to 73 ("Unlawful Drilling", "Duels" (repealed), "Forcible Entry and Detainer").
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) / NOTHING (not covered): see the header of ccc2-treason.l4 and NOTES.md.

§ `Section 70 -- Unlawful drilling: orders by the Governor in Council`

-- Subsection (1): "The Governor in Council may, by proclamation, make orders (a) to prohibit assemblies, without lawful authority, of persons for the purpose (i) of training or drilling themselves,
-- (ii) of being trained or drilled to the use of arms, or (iii) of practising military exercises; or (b) to prohibit persons when assembled for any purpose from training or drilling themselves or from
-- being trained or drilled." A power of an official, encoded for what it means to the person: which orders there can be.
-- src:1102 | Orders by Governor in Council
-- src:1103 | 70 (1) The Governor in Council may, by proclamation, make orders
-- src:1104 | (a) to prohibit assemblies, without lawful authority, of persons for the purpose
-- src:1105 | (i) of training or drilling themselves,
-- src:1106 | (ii) of being trained or drilled to the use of arms, or
-- src:1107 | (iii) of practising military exercises; or
-- src:1108 | (b) to prohibit persons when assembled for any purpose from training or drilling themselves or from being trained or drilled.
@ref Criminal Code s 70(1) (orders by Governor in Council) (src:1102-1108)
DECLARE `s 70(1) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 70(1)(a)(i) an order prohibiting assemblies, without lawful authority, of persons for the purpose of training or drilling themselves`
    `s 70(1)(a)(ii) an order prohibiting assemblies, without lawful authority, of persons for the purpose of being trained or drilled to the use of arms`
    `s 70(1)(a)(iii) an order prohibiting assemblies, without lawful authority, of persons for the purpose of practising military exercises`
    `s 70(1)(b) an order prohibiting persons when assembled for any purpose from training or drilling themselves or from being trained or drilled`
    `s 70(1) an order of another kind`

@ref Criminal Code s 70(1) (orders by Governor in Council) (src:1102-1108)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 70(1) kind of order`
      `the order is made by the Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made by proclamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(1) the Governor in Council may make the order` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `s 70(1) an order of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make orders (a) to prohibit assemblies ... (b) to prohibit persons when assembled"
    ELSE IF `the order is made by the Governor in Council` AND `the order is made by proclamation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Governor in Council may, by proclamation, make orders"

-- The same power as a regulative rule: a permission that lapses without consequence if unused (the default of MAY).
@ref Criminal Code s 70(1) (orders by Governor in Council) (src:1102-1108)
DECLARE `s 70(1) act` IS ONE OF `s 70(1) makes an order by proclamation`

@ref Criminal Code s 70(1) (orders by Governor in Council) (src:1102-1108)
`s 70(1) the power of the Governor in Council` MEANS
    PARTY `the Governor in Council`
    MAY `s 70(1) makes an order by proclamation`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Subsection (2): "An order that is made under subsection (1) may be general or may be made applicable to particular places, districts or assemblies to be specified in the order."
-- src:1109 | General or special order
-- src:1110 | (2) An order that is made under subsection (1) may be general or may be made applicable to particular places, districts or assemblies to be specified in the order.
@ref Criminal Code s 70(2) (general or special order) (src:1109-1110)
GIVEN `the order is general` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made applicable to particular places, districts or assemblies specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place, district or assembly is one specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(2) the order applies to the place, district or assembly` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order is general` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the order is made applicable to particular places, districts or assemblies specified in the order` AND `the place, district or assembly is one specified in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be general or may be made applicable to particular places, districts or assemblies to be specified in the order"

-- Subsection (3): "Every person who contravenes an order made under this section is guilty of (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or (b) an offence
-- punishable on summary conviction."
-- src:1111 | Punishment
-- src:1112 | (3) Every person who contravenes an order made under this section is guilty of
-- src:1113 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:1114 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 70(3) (punishment) (src:1111-1114)
GIVEN `s 70(1) the Governor in Council may make the order: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 70(2) the order applies to the place, district or assembly: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 70(3) the person contravenes an order made under section 70` MEANS
    IF `s 70(1) the Governor in Council may make the order: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `s 70(2) the order applies to the place, district or assembly: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        AND `the person contravenes the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who contravenes an order made under this section"

@ref Criminal Code s 70(3) (punishment) (src:1111-1114)
`s 70(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 70(3) (punishment) (src:1111-1114)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 70(3) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

