§ `Sections 72 and 73 -- Forcible entry and detainer`

-- Subsection (1): "A person commits forcible entry when that person enters real property that is in the actual and peaceable possession of another in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace
-- or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace." "When" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05): a failed condition is JUST FALSE (fork F11).
-- src:1120 | Forcible entry
-- src:1121 | 72 (1) A person commits forcible entry when that person enters real property that is in the actual and peaceable possession of another in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace.
@ref Criminal Code s 72(1) (forcible entry) (src:1120-1121)
GIVEN `the person enters real property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is in the actual and peaceable possession of another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enters in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry` MEANS
    IF `the person enters real property` AND `the property is in the actual and peaceable possession of another` AND `the person enters in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits forcible entry when that person enters real property that is in the actual and peaceable possession of another in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace"

-- Subsection (1.1): "For the purposes of subsection (1), it is immaterial whether or not a person is entitled to enter the real property or whether or not that person has any intention of taking possession
-- of the real property." So `s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry` reads neither fact. A flat negative: JUST FALSE for "is it material".
-- src:1122 | Matters not material
-- src:1123 | (1.1) For the purposes of subsection (1), it is immaterial whether or not a person is entitled to enter the real property or whether or not that person has any intention of taking possession of the real property.
@ref Criminal Code s 72(1.1) (matters not material) (src:1122-1123)
GIVEN `the question arises for the purposes of subsection 72(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(1.1) the person's entitlement to enter the real property, or intention of taking possession of it, is material` MEANS
    IF `the question arises for the purposes of subsection 72(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is immaterial whether or not a person is entitled to enter the real property or whether or not that person has any intention of taking possession of the real property"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (1)"

-- Subsection (2): "A person commits forcible detainer when, being in actual possession of real property without colour of right, he detains it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace
-- or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace, against a person who is entitled by law to possession of it."
-- src:1124 | Forcible detainer
-- src:1125 | (2) A person commits forcible detainer when, being in actual possession of real property without colour of right, he detains it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace, against a person who is entitled by law to possession of it.
@ref Criminal Code s 72(2) (forcible detainer) (src:1124-1125)
GIVEN `the person is in actual possession of real property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is without colour of right` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person detains it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person detains it against a person who is entitled by law to possession of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(2) the person commits forcible detainer` MEANS
    IF `the person is in actual possession of real property` AND `the person is without colour of right`
        AND `the person detains it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace or reasonable apprehension of a breach of the peace`
        AND `the person detains it against a person who is entitled by law to possession of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits forcible detainer when, being in actual possession of real property without colour of right, he detains it in a manner that is likely to cause a breach of the peace"

-- Subsection (3): "The questions whether a person is in actual and peaceable possession or is in actual possession without colour of right are questions of law." A classification of the two questions;
-- any other question is not covered (the court, not a witness, answers these two: a person cannot state them as facts, so a seat layer asks the underlying facts and states the question as the person's own view).
-- src:1126 | Questions of law
-- src:1127 | (3) The questions whether a person is in actual and peaceable possession or is in actual possession without colour of right are questions of law.
@ref Criminal Code s 72(3) (questions of law) (src:1126-1127)
DECLARE `s 72(3) question` IS ONE OF
    `s 72(3) whether a person is in actual and peaceable possession`
    `s 72(3) whether a person is in actual possession without colour of right`
    `s 72(3) another question`

@ref Criminal Code s 72(3) (questions of law) (src:1126-1127)
GIVEN question IS A `s 72(3) question`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72(3) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    CONSIDER question
    WHEN `s 72(3) whether a person is in actual and peaceable possession` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 72(3) whether a person is in actual possession without colour of right` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 72(3) another question` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection classifies only the two questions it names

-- src:1128 | Punishment
-- src:1129 | 73 Every person who commits forcible entry or forcible detainer is guilty of
-- src:1130 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:1131 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 73 (punishment) (src:1128-1131)
GIVEN `s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 72(2) the person commits forcible detainer: the answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73 the person commits forcible entry or forcible detainer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 72(2) the person commits forcible detainer: the answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 72(1) the person commits forcible entry: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `s 72(2) the person commits forcible detainer: the answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits forcible entry when" and "A person commits forcible detainer when" (section 72)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who commits forcible entry or forcible detainer"

@ref Criminal Code s 73 (punishment) (src:1128-1131)
`s 73 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 73 (punishment) (src:1128-1131)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 73 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`), `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
